  "lineage": "Early-2000s UK electronic subgenre developed in West London through producers IG Culture, Bugz in the Attic, and 4hero. Characterized by complex broken-rhythm percussion (often 6/4 or 9/8 polymetric framework), jazz-and-soul-vocal integration, deep-house-and-techno harmonic vocabulary, and the canonical 4-and-7-Records label. Distinguished from drum-and-bass by broken beat's slower tempo and explicit jazz-house-fusion orientation.",
